msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-heli-parts-list.rst:13
#: 52859b08a74d46e0ab2b0b2d7256115f
msgid "RC helicopter frame"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-heli-parts-list.rst:15
#: ab351c2b419f4680ac9ad7bfbce0ba8a
msgid "ArduPilot supports single rotor with conventional or direct drive tail, tandem rotor, or collective pitch quad-rotor helicopter frames."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-heli-parts-list.rst:18
#: c7e68b5af5b74844adcb0205b2e697a8
msgid "The program can be configured to fly flybar or flybarless, with CCPM swash mixing or single-servo (H1) swash types. The system has flown helicopters ranging from micro size with a Pixracer to large piston and turbine powered machines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-heli-parts-list.rst:24
#: b1043bfb76c34e6bb925bb2166fa60c4
msgid "8-channel Transmitter / Receiver"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-heli-parts-list.rst:26
#: 990d4e5f2d9b42c6a0c7b6993c993bb6
msgid "Your transmitter & receiver must support minimum 8 channels (elevator, aileron, collective pitch, rudder, flight mode, tuning knob, auxiliary function switch, throttle hold)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-heli-parts-list.rst:31
#: 62106a6556ab45da9786d5ffccca342f
msgid "Use of electric and engine governors"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-heli-parts-list.rst:33
#: 54d2c164654c429e8e840a647a230519
msgid "If you intend to use any Copter flight control modes other than Acro and Stabilize, it is recommended that the speed controller you purchase for an electric helicopter have a governor mode. For piston and turbine engines a governor is required. This is because Copter will be controlling the pitch of the main blades automatically along with its internal throttle control system. The throttle curve in ArduPilot will be used for fallback and feedforward for piston and turbine engines in the event the governor fails in flight, and for faster governor response on high collective pitch loading."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-heli-parts-list.rst:42
#: a7851858881b44b4a9ad86de56bd5e4b
msgid "For electric helicopters ArduPilot will set the throttle for the ESC governor to hold the headspeed constant at all times."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-heli-parts-list.rst:46
#: 2dce4992e4084125ba9ddec83907e70f
msgid "Digital servos"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-heli-parts-list.rst:48
#: b6cb12b87e4e47f69e9e5c95b9770fb2
msgid "You should use digital servos instead of analog. Digital servos have much faster response time, more accurate positioning, and your helicopter will fly much more accurate and stable with digital servos."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-heli-parts-list.rst:53
#: 5ee4169df9ee4c2793f748fc6aa33b35
msgid "Batteries"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/traditional-heli-parts-list.rst:55
#: 04441c2812e74748a4c6721bd438b5cf
msgid "There are no special requirements for flight batteries. However, as a general rule, it is safer if you can have a separate motor battery and radio battery on electric helicopters. Electric motor power systems can have very high power draw in helicopters. Having separate batteries will prevent \"brownout\" of power to the flight electronics."
msgstr ""
